acts/PrevCDRs.htm\\\">\\\"Previous Commanders\\\"</a>. USSOUTHCOM. Archived from <a rel=\\\"nofollow\\\" class=\\\"external text\\\" href=\\\"http://www.southcom.mil/pa/Facts/PrevCDRs.htm\\\">the original</a> on 4 November 2002<span class=\\\"reference-accessdate\\\">. Retrieved <span class=\\\"nowrap\\\">30 September</span> 2016</span>.</cite><span title=\\\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Previous+Commanders&amp;rft.pub=USSOUTHCOM&amp;rft&#95;id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.southcom.mil%2Fpa%2FFacts%2FPrevCDRs.htm&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3APanama+Canal+Department\\\" class=\\\"Z3988\\\"></span></span>\\n</li>\\n<li id=\\\"cite&#95;note-FOOTNOTEClay2010a92-8\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-cite-backlink\\\"><b><a href=\\\"#cite_ref-FOOTNOTEClay2010a92_8-0\\\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\\\"reference-text\\\"><a href=\\\"#CITEREFClay2010a\\\">Clay 2010a</a>, p.&#160;92.</span>\\n</li>\\n</ol></div>\\n<ul><li><link rel=\\\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\\\" href=\\\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\\\" /><cite id=\\\"CITEREFArSouth\\\" class=\\\"citation web cs1\\\">ArSouth. <a rel=\\\"nofollow\\\" class=\\\"external text\\\" href=\\\"https://www.arsouth.army.mil/About-Us/history/\\\">\\\"U.S. Army South – A Brief History\\\"</a>.</cite><span title=\\\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=U.S.+Army+South+%E2%80%93+A+Brief+History&amp;rft.au=ArSouth&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.arsouth.army.mil%2FAbout-Us%2Fhistory%2F&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3APanama+Canal+Department\\\" class=\\\"Z3988\\\"></span></li>\\n<li><link rel=\\\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\\\" href=\\\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\\\" /><cite id=\\\"CITEREFClay2010a\\\" class=\\\"citation book cs1\\\">Clay, Steven E. (2010a). <a rel=\\\"nofollow\\\" class=\\\"external text\\\" href=\\\"http://cgsc.contentdm.oclc.org/cdm/singleitem/collection/p16040coll3/id/198/rec/3\\\"><i>US Army Order of Battle 1919–1941</i></a>. Vol.&#160;1. Fort Leavenworth, Kansas: Combat Studies Institute Press. <a href=\\\"/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)\\\" class=\\\"mw-redirect\\\" title=\\\"ISBN (identifier)\\\">ISBN</a>&#160;<a href=\\\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/9780984190140\\\" title=\\\"Special:BookSources/9780984190140\\\"><bdi>9780984190140</bdi></a>.</cite><span title=\\\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=US+Army+Order+of+Battle+1919%E2%80%931941&amp;rft.place=Fort+Leavenworth%2C+Kansas&amp;rft.pub=Combat+Studies+Institute+Press&amp;rft.date=2010&amp;rft.isbn=9780984190140&amp;rft.aulast=Clay&amp;rft.aufirst=Steven+E.&amp;rft&#95;id=http%3A%2F%2Fcgsc.contentdm.oclc.org%2Fcdm%2Fsingleitem%2Fcollection%2Fp16040coll3%2Fid%2F198%2Frec%2F3&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3APanama+Canal+Department\\\" class=\\\"Z3988\\\"></span></li>\\n<li><link rel=\\\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\\\" href=\\\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\\\" /><cite id=\\\"CITEREFConn&#95;Engelman&#95;Fairchild1964\\\" class=\\\"citation book cs1\\\">Conn Engelman Fairchild (1964). <i>The United States Army in World War II: The Western Hemisphere: Guarding the United States and its Outposts</i>. Washington, D.C.: Centre of Military History.</cite><span title=\\\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=The+United+States+Army+in+World+War+II%3A+The+Western+Hemisphere%3A+Guarding+the+United+States+and+its+Outposts&amp;rft.place=Washington%2C+D.C.&amp;rft.pub=Centre+of+Military+History&amp;rft.date=1964&amp;rft.au=Conn+Engelman+Fairchild&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3APanama+Canal+Department\\\" class=\\\"Z3988\\\"></span> Authors were Stetson Conn, Rose Engelman, and Byron Fairchild. Department of the Army, 1964. 593 pp.</li>\\n<li><link rel=\\\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\\\" href=\\\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\\\" /><cite id=\\\"CITEREFSouthCom2006\\\" class=\\\"citation web cs1\\\">SouthCom (11 September 2006). <a rel=\\\"nofollow\\\" class=\\\"external text\\\" href=\\\"https://web.archive.org/web/20081017213112/http://www.southcom.mil/PA/Facts/History.htm\\\">\\\"U.S. Southern Command History\\\"</a>. <i>USSOUTHCOM</i>. Archived from <a rel=\\\"nofollow\\\" class=\\\"external text\\\" href=\\\"http://www.southcom.mil:80/PA/Facts/History.htm\\\">the original</a> on 17 October 2008<span class=\\\"reference-accessdate\\\">. Retrieved <span class=\\\"nowrap\\\">1 February</span> 2017</span>.</cite><span title=\\\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=USSOUTHCOM&amp;rft.atitle=U.S.+Southern+Command+History&amp;rft.date=2006-09-11&amp;rft.au=SouthCom&amp;rft&#95;id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.southcom.mil%3A80%2FPA%2FFacts%2FHistory.htm&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3APanama+Canal+Department\\\" class=\\\"Z3988\\\"></span></li></ul>\\n<div class=\\\"mw-heading mw-heading2\\\"><h2 id=\\\"Further_reading\\\">Further reading</h2></div>\\n<ul><li><link rel=\\\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\\\" href=\\\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\\\" /><cite id=\\\"CITEREFUnited&#95;States&#95;Army1947\\\" class=\\\"citation book cs1\\\">United States Army (1947). <i>History of the Panama Canal Department</i>. Quarry Heights, Canal Zone: Historical Section, Caribbean Defense Command. <a href=\\\"/wiki/OCLC_(identifier)\\\" class=\\\"mw-redirect\\\" title=\\\"OCLC (identifier)\\\">OCLC</a>&#160;<a rel=\\\"nofollow\\\" class=\\\"external text\\\" href=\\\"https://search.worldcat.org/oclc/3698244\\\">3698244</a>.</cite><span title=\\\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=History+of+the+Panama+Canal+Department&amp;rft.place=Quarry+Heights%2C+Canal+Zone&amp;rft.pub=Historical+Section%2C+Caribbean+Defense+Command&amp;rft.date=1947&amp;rft&#95;id=info%3Aoclcnum%2F3698244&amp;rft.au=United+States+Army&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3APanama+Canal+Department\\\" class=\\\"Z3988\\\"></span> – 4 volumes</li></ul></div>\"}}"}